[[Ashinohara]] has a Threnodian whose power comes and goes in predictable cycles. It caused Honami City to vanish with a then-new power, and thus is implicated in the recent disappearance of Ashinohara as a whole.

[[Chongzhou]] is known to have a Threnodian.

An ancient civilisation preserved in the [[Somnoire]] also contains the Threnodian which destroyed said civilisation, as it slipped inside and eventually caused the fracturing of the Somnoire into its present day layers. As this Threnodian attempted to reconstruct both itself and the shattered memories of the civilisation, it has gained a soul and is now known as [[D]], master of the cinema layer - although the [[The White Tower|original Threnodian]] may still exist, sealed inside.

==Trivia==
===Etymology===
*'Threnodian' is an adjective that refers to something that is mournful or related to a threnody, which is a song, poem, or speech expressing sorrow, especially for someone who has died. It often describes artistic expression that embodies themes of grief or lamentation.